  "task": {
    "objective": "Develop canal districts through farming, crossings, levees and physical cargo; balance district interests with downstream water and shared flood/navigation effects.",
    "natural_termination": "No early success/failure condition. The finite 768-turn charter ends by truncation. Already-terminal raw calls preserve state/clock and return zero rewards.",
    "interaction": "Sluice releases travel through a three-slot downstream queue. Irrigation competes for navigation water. Exchangeable equipment, physical cargo, finite commissions, bridge/berth congestion and delayed downstream effects connect crews.",
    "observation_access": "Public static map. Dynamic groups use Manhattan radius5, nearest-distance then id order, capped at8 citizens or3 per object group. Visible attributes equal native slot contents; unseen slots are zero. Only keepers receive home incoming-water totals remotely. Town readings are local and may be stale."
  },
